---
/** What Huddle is, for whom, where it runs and how people get in: a lead line over four columns. */
---

<section class="intro wrap" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
  <h2 id="intro-title" class="sr-only">What Huddle is</h2>
  <div data-reveal>
    <p class="lead-line">
      Huddle is team chat you run yourself: channels, threads, direct messages, files and search, on your
      own Cloudflare account and its free plan. The code is open under the MIT licence, and your data stays
      in your account.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="cols" data-reveal>
    <p><b>For small teams.</b> Studios, agencies, clubs, schools, charities and companies of a few to a few hundred people who want proper team chat without a monthly bill for every person or someone else's terms on their history.</p>
    <p><b>Everything you expect.</b> Public and private channels, direct messages, threads, reactions, @mentions, files, full search, unread counts, push notifications and email summaries, with owners, admins, members and guests.</p>
    <p><b>On your own account.</b> Huddle, your messages and your files all live in your own Cloudflare account. No company sits in the middle reading or selling your data. There isn't a Huddle company at all.</p>
    <p><b>Phone-code sign-in.</b> People sign in with a six-digit code from an authenticator app, or an emailed code if you turn email on. There are no passwords to leak, and an invite link decides who gets in.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .intro {
    padding-block: var(--section) 96px;
  }
  .lead-line {
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.2vw, 32px);
    line-height: 1.22;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 24px;
    margin-top: 72px;
  }
  .cols p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .cols b {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 40px 20px;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .lead-line {
      font-size: 21px;
    }
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 28px;
      margin-top: 48px;
    }
  }
</style>
